.TH "CONTROL" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
control \- interactively control a radiod receiver channel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B control
.RI "[-v] [-V] [-s ssrc] [-r seconds] [radio]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
control discovers radiod instances or connects to a specified control/status
destination, selects a receiver channel, and displays its state with an
interactive "ncurses" text interface.
It can change nearly any channel parameter.
This only controls the receiver; use the separate "monitor" command
to listen to its output.
Unsupported or invalid settings are ignored.
Channel control is *not* exclusive; "control" can coexist on the same channel with other instances
or user interfaces.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-s ssrc"
Select a channel SSRC. Without this option the program produces a list of active
channels and prompts for a selection or the creation of a new channel.
.TP
.B "\-r seconds"
Set initial status refresh/poll interval in seconds. Default 0.25.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH INTERACTION
Press h or ? for the installed keyboard help. Use Tab and navigation keys to
select fields; left/right select a digit and up/down change it. Frequently
used commands include f for frequency, m or p for preset, e
for encoding, g for gain, and q to quit. Ctrl-L redraws the display.
.PP
Without a radio argument, the program browses _ka9q-ctl._udp services through
multicast service discovery (eg, Avahi).
Discovery requires the Avahi tools and appropriate network
reachability. Explicitly specifying the control destination avoids interactive
service selection.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
LANG selects the locale. A locale with digit grouping, such as en_US.UTF-8, is
recommended for the interactive frequency display.
.SH FILES
share/ka9q-radio/help.txt under the installation prefix on the system running control
contains keyboard
help.
Presets come from /usr/[local/]share/ka9q-radio/presets.conf on the system running radiod.
.SH EXAMPLES
Discover an instance or select a particular channel directly:
.PP
.nf
control
control \-s 10000000 hf.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), tune(1), monitor(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
